---
import LandingLayout from '@/layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import { rentalTerms } from '@/data/rental-terms';
import { fleet } from '@/data/fleet';

const urus = fleet.find((c) => c.name === 'Lamborghini Urus');
const evo = fleet.find((c) => c.name === 'Huracan EVO');
const { deposit, mileage, minimumAge } = rentalTerms;

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Urus or Huracan EVO — which should I book?',
    a: `Count your passengers first. The Urus has four doors, a boot and enough ground clearance for hotel ramps, so it copes with an airport pickup or a group. The Huracan seats two and swallows about one carry-on. Pick it when the drive itself is the plan.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I put suitcases in the Huracan EVO?',
    a: 'Barely. Storage is a small front compartment with no rear cargo area at all, so budget for roughly one carry-on plus a soft bag between two people. Arriving from the airport with full-size luggage is a job for the Urus.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does a Lamborghini rental include?',
    a: `Both cars come with ${mileage.includedPerDay} miles for each day of the booking, pooled rather than capped daily, and both take the same refundable ${deposit.display} deposit. You need to be ${minimumAge} or over with your own qualifying insurance.`,
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};
---
<LandingLayout
  title="Lamborghini Rental Miami | Lussaro Collection"
  description="Rent Lamborghinis in Miami with Lussaro Collection. Select from Huracán, STO, Urus and more for premium exotic car experiences."
  h1="Lamborghini Rental Miami"
  intro="Two Lamborghinis, and they are not interchangeable. One is an SUV you could genuinely use all week; the other is a two-seat V10 that exists to be driven."
  only={["lamborghini-urus", "huracan-evo"]}
  fullFleetLink
  ctaTitle="Reserve your Lamborghini"
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <h2>Two very different Lamborghinis</h2>
  <p>Most people picture the coupe. Worth knowing the two cars we run solve opposite problems, and the wrong choice is the one that ruins the day.</p>

  <h3><a href="/cars/lamborghini-urus">Lamborghini Urus</a> — ${urus.price.toLocaleString()}/day</h3>
  <p>Four doors, a proper boot of around 616 litres, and the ride height to get over a speed bump or up a hotel ramp without drama. It is the only car we run that carries people and cases while still sounding like a Lamborghini, courtesy of a twin-turbo V8 driving all four wheels. Rated {urus.power} hp with a {urus.zeroToSixty} sprint to 60 mph.</p>

  <h3><a href="/cars/huracan-evo">Lamborghini Huracan EVO</a> — ${evo.price.toLocaleString()}/day</h3>
  <p>Strictly two seats, a small front trunk, and a naturally aspirated V10 with no hybrid assistance and no quiet mode — it is loud from cold start, by design. The front splitter sits low, so steep driveways want a slow, angled approach. It is not a sensible car, and does not pretend to be.</p>

  <h2>Choosing by occasion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Airport arrival with luggage</strong> — Urus, comfortably.</li>
    <li><strong>Dinner reservation for four</strong> — Urus again; the Huracan physically cannot.</li>
    <li><strong>A photo or video shoot</strong> — the Huracan, for the shape and the noise.</li>
    <li><strong>A weekend where the driving is the point</strong> — Huracan.</li>
    <li><strong>One car for a whole week</strong> — Urus, without hesitating.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Terms, briefly</h2>
  <p>Each booking carries {mileage.includedPerDay} miles per day, added up across the rental rather than reset every morning. A refundable {deposit.display} deposit is taken when the booking is confirmed and returned after the car is checked over on the way back. Drivers must be {minimumAge} or over, hold a valid licence, and carry insurance covering the vehicle — or buy a daily policy from us. Multi-day rates and every other figure are on the <a href="/pricing">rate card</a>. For the rest of what we run, start at <a href="/exotic-car-rental-miami">exotic car rental in Miami</a>.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  {faqs.map((f) => (
    <>
      <h3>{f.q}</h3>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </>
  ))}
</LandingLayout>
